  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/36af7324fd2112d94feddc5a1a02a91d97bbc0866cb93a6ca711dd73f566305a.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$",
  "worked_solution": "The diagonal $\\overset{\u2015}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $\u25b3ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/7cfcb5cdf77b4afbf25afd64e37bb33f0ab2c211e09659181bfc16db0ccd2db7.png)\n\n Computing the area of $\u25b3ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(18)(8)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{70}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =72\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061{70}^{\u2218} \\\\  & \u224867.658,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 67.658 \\\\  & =135.316.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $135.$",
